  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\nIssued at 116 PM CST WED NOV 18 2026\n\nUpper level low along the Gulf coast today is forecast to lift\nnorthward, fill in, and then get caught up in the southern jet\nover the course of the next 48 hours. Most of the models, and\nmulti-model blends, keep the bulk of the deeper moisture\nassociated with this system to our south and east. The \ndeterministic run of the GFS is a bit more aggressive in bringing\nmoisture up our way, and so its rain chances are noticeably\nhigher. We will keep the POPs for central Alabama closer to the\nensemble/model blend solutions, which is no more than 20-30\npercent through the weekend. A moisture starved cold front is\nforecast to push through the state late Sunday/Sunday night.\nSurface high pressure builds back to our north after that, which\nmeans more dry weather for the start of next week. All-in-all,\nthere does not appear to be anything of high impact for our area\nover the next 7 days.\n\n/61/",
